1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,198
The library has a quiet reading corner for us.

2
00:00:04,448 --> 00:00:07,760
And three books that need to go back.

3
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,550
A fine journey for a Saturday.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,498
Three books coming home sounds like a fair
trade.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,129
Red, blue, yellow. All three returns are here.

6
00:00:19,379 --> 00:00:21,316
Nothing under the island.

7
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:24,349
Good. Even the floor is ready.

8
00:00:24,599 --> 00:00:29,497
Good. None of the return books are hiding
under our feet.

9
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,724
Three adult tickets and three child tickets.
Nine dollars, already paid.

10
00:00:34,974 --> 00:00:37,739
Then my wallet gets a quiet trip.

11
00:00:37,989 --> 00:00:40,754
Until we come home. These are one-way.

12
00:00:41,004 --> 00:00:44,498
We'll plan that trip when it's time to leave.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,190
Route seven, nine fifty. I have the time.

14
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,270
And the destination is the library.

15
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:54,490
We need both parts.

16
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:59,290
Library first, then the time. I'll try saying
it together.

17
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:03,330
It might rain on our books.

18
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:06,840
We can be ready without opening it.

19
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:09,490
My hair appreciates that policy.

20
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:14,290
What about the dinosaur? I hope its book stays
dry.

21
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:19,129
Cards stay with me. Books stay with Leo.

22
00:01:19,379 --> 00:01:21,739
And tickets stay with Dan.

23
00:01:21,989 --> 00:01:24,772
Three jobs. No guessing which pocket.

24
00:01:25,022 --> 00:01:29,497
I'll keep the backpack close. Books are my
department today.

25
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,283
I want a book of maps.

26
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:36,739
I want to see how seeds grow.

27
00:01:36,989 --> 00:01:40,195
Mine should have a very large dinosaur.

28
00:01:40,445 --> 00:01:44,497
Three very different readers. That sounds like
our family.

29
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,426
Early, organized, and all six of us.

30
00:01:48,676 --> 00:01:51,988
Let us keep that last part all day.

31
00:01:52,238 --> 00:01:54,778
The dinosaur can wait for us.

32
00:01:55,028 --> 00:01:59,498
I don't think any of my seeds will run away
either.

33
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,283
Here we are. Ten minutes early.

34
00:02:03,533 --> 00:02:06,739
There is another stop across the street.

35
00:02:06,989 --> 00:02:10,195
A neighborhood can be very well supplied.

36
00:02:10,445 --> 00:02:14,497
Maybe they're only well supplied in the other
direction.

37
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,040
I may have mastered arriving early.

38
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:21,216
My wrist says we are extremely early.

39
00:02:21,466 --> 00:02:24,778
Now let us check where we are going.

40
00:02:25,028 --> 00:02:29,498
Fair point. A watch can't tell us which stop
to use.

41
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,293
It says seven.

42
00:02:32,543 --> 00:02:35,790
And there is another line under it.

43
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:39,716
My excellent plan appears to have small print.

44
00:02:39,966 --> 00:02:44,498
Let's read that smaller line before we pick
this bench.

45
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:49,017
Does the other bench get a different bus?

46
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:52,374
It gets buses going the other way.

47
00:02:52,624 --> 00:02:55,321
That sounds like an important difference.

48
00:02:55,571 --> 00:02:59,498
So the benches look alike, but the rides
don't?

49
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,607
Nine fifty here too. That is reassuring.

50
00:03:03,857 --> 00:03:06,554
Check the heading above the time.

51
00:03:06,804 --> 00:03:10,321
Two buses can leave at the same minute.

52
00:03:10,571 --> 00:03:14,498
And my watch wouldn't know which one I meant.

53
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,377
Our sign says River.

54
00:03:17,627 --> 00:03:21,144
The library does have a book about rivers.

55
00:03:21,394 --> 00:03:25,321
But we would like the building with the books.

56
00:03:25,571 --> 00:03:29,498
I'd rather read that river book inside the
library.

57
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,197
Could the library come here instead?

58
00:03:33,447 --> 00:03:36,144
It would need an enormous ticket.

59
00:03:36,394 --> 00:03:39,091
We can make the smaller journey.

60
00:03:39,341 --> 00:03:44,498
Good. I don't think a whole building fits
through the bus door.

61
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,787
Bakery behind us, crossing ahead.

62
00:03:48,037 --> 00:03:50,734
The library is north of here.

63
00:03:50,984 --> 00:03:54,911
My time was right. My side may not be.

64
00:03:55,161 --> 00:03:59,498
The bakery's a better clue than your watch
this time.

65
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,812
Did the stop move while we were walking?

66
00:04:04,062 --> 00:04:07,374
No. I brought us to the wrong side.

67
00:04:07,624 --> 00:04:10,164
Then we can change sides carefully.

68
00:04:10,414 --> 00:04:14,498
Good. It would be hard to carry the whole
stop.

69
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:20,247
The right bus number can still take us the
wrong way.

70
00:04:20,497 --> 00:04:22,374
Right number, wrong direction.

71
00:04:22,624 --> 00:04:25,321
We caught it before getting on.

72
00:04:25,571 --> 00:04:29,498
I'd rather look a little silly on this
sidewalk.

73
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:33,040
We still have time to check.

74
00:04:33,290 --> 00:04:35,830
The crossing is at the intersection.

75
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:40,164
And if we miss this bus, we wait. No racing.

76
00:04:40,414 --> 00:04:44,498
Good. The library books can wait an extra few
minutes.

77
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,900
We are beside the bakery.

78
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:51,410
We want the library near Oak Street.

79
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:54,920
Those are useful things to tell someone.

80
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:59,290
Grandpa would know which side we mean from
that.

81
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:04,843
My dad knows this street. We can describe
where we are.

82
00:05:05,093 --> 00:05:07,561
Grandpa Ed can check our thinking.

83
00:05:07,811 --> 00:05:10,654
Tell him the stop has not moved.

84
00:05:10,904 --> 00:05:14,497
I think he'll want to hear the destination
first.

85
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:18,630
Route seven, bakery side. We want the library.

86
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:22,010
That gives Dad something clear to work with.

87
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:25,754
Better than saying we are beside a bus stop.

88
00:05:26,004 --> 00:05:29,498
Good. I'll say where we want to go, too.

89
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,719
Are the cards still here?

90
00:05:32,969 --> 00:05:35,585
Yes. Zipped in the same place.

91
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:40,042
Good. We are fixing one small mistake, not
starting three.

92
00:05:40,292 --> 00:05:44,499
One mistake is plenty to keep us busy this
morning.

93
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:48,550
I can see Library across the street.

94
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,484
That is encouraging.

95
00:05:50,734 --> 00:05:55,393
We will read the whole sign when we reach that
side.

96
00:05:55,643 --> 00:05:59,498
This time let's read the big and little words.

97
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:03,607
These two dots are the two stops.

98
00:06:03,857 --> 00:06:06,964
And this marked crossing connects the
sidewalks.

99
00:06:07,214 --> 00:06:10,321
A very useful line between two dots.

100
00:06:10,571 --> 00:06:14,498
We'll use that crossing when we're ready, all
together.

101
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,968
Did we spoil our library day?

102
00:06:18,218 --> 00:06:21,811
Not at all. We found a small problem early.

103
00:06:22,061 --> 00:06:25,654
And we have a careful way to fix it.

104
00:06:25,904 --> 00:06:29,497
Good. I was worried my dinosaur might miss me.

105
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:34,359
Hi, Dad. Have you a minute for a direction
check?

106
00:06:34,609 --> 00:06:38,103
We found the right number and an interesting
problem.

107
00:06:38,353 --> 00:06:41,118
I'll tell him which side we're on.

108
00:06:41,368 --> 00:06:44,498
Start with the bakery. That's easy to spot.

109
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:49,359
I wanted this to be the outing with no
mistakes.

110
00:06:49,609 --> 00:06:52,739
You brought us early enough to notice one.

111
00:06:52,989 --> 00:06:55,024
And we are still together.

112
00:06:55,274 --> 00:06:59,498
I do like that part. We can work it out
together.

113
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:04,724
We are at the bakery stop. The panel says
southbound, River.

114
00:07:04,974 --> 00:07:08,468
Hello, travelers. And where do you want to
arrive?

115
00:07:08,718 --> 00:07:10,753
The library on Oak Street.

116
00:07:11,003 --> 00:07:14,497
That's the part we want to get right, Dad.

117
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:20,159
Check the destination on your leaflet. What
direction does it name?

118
00:07:20,409 --> 00:07:22,093
Northbound, Library.

119
00:07:22,343 --> 00:07:24,991
That matches the map’s north arrow.

120
00:07:25,241 --> 00:07:29,498
Good. The leaflet and the map tell the same
story.

121
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:33,116
Do we need bus eight instead?

122
00:07:33,366 --> 00:07:38,368
Seven goes both ways here. Check the
destination on the bus too.

123
00:07:38,618 --> 00:07:40,439
We will. Thanks, Dad.

124
00:07:40,689 --> 00:07:44,498
Same number, different place. I can look for
Library.

125
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,630
We will check the sign ourselves before
boarding.

126
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:52,374
Enjoy the library. Save a good story for me.

127
00:07:52,624 --> 00:07:55,389
First, let us reach that crossing together.

128
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:59,498
Bye, Dad. We'll save you the story of both
stops.

129
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:03,343
Could you check the direction with me?

130
00:08:03,593 --> 00:08:06,811
Yes. We can look at the same thing.

131
00:08:07,061 --> 00:08:10,654
Then we will all know why it is right.

132
00:08:10,904 --> 00:08:14,497
Good. I like hearing how you figured it out.

133
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:18,718
We are going away from the bus stop.

134
00:08:18,968 --> 00:08:23,311
For a short walk that takes us to the right
one.

135
00:08:23,561 --> 00:08:25,654
Why the long way around?

136
00:08:25,904 --> 00:08:29,497
That's where we can cross together at the
signal.

137
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,184
I pressed it.

138
00:08:32,434 --> 00:08:35,484
Now we wait for the walking signal.

139
00:08:35,734 --> 00:08:39,991
The button asks. It does not stop every car
itself.

140
00:08:40,241 --> 00:08:44,498
Got it. My finger asked and my feet can wait.

141
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:48,718
Will the library be angry if we wait?

142
00:08:48,968 --> 00:08:51,436
Libraries are very good at waiting.

143
00:08:51,686 --> 00:08:55,279
And we have another bus if we need one.

144
00:08:55,529 --> 00:08:59,497
Good. I wouldn't want to run with all those
books.

145
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:04,190
Walking signal. Check that the cars have
stopped.

146
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,240
Clear this way.

147
00:09:06,490 --> 00:09:08,890
And clear here. Together now.

148
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:13,690
With you, Mom. The books are coming across
with us.

149
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,900
This stop is getting closer.

150
00:09:18,150 --> 00:09:21,410
We are the part that is moving.

151
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:23,630
Is everybody still together?

152
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:27,570
Yes, keep walking till we're on the sidewalk.

153
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,911
The blue shelter is a little way back.

154
00:09:34,161 --> 00:09:35,982
Along the sidewalk now.

155
00:09:36,232 --> 00:09:39,643
A longer safe path was a good path.

156
00:09:39,893 --> 00:09:44,497
And we can see the shelter without stepping
off the curb.

157
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:48,116
Our old bench is still there.

158
00:09:48,366 --> 00:09:50,585
Exactly where we left it.

159
00:09:50,835 --> 00:09:55,042
Now we will check the sign before choosing the
bench.

160
00:09:55,292 --> 00:09:59,499
It'd be nice if this bench came with
directions too.

161
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,300
Seven. Northbound. Library.

162
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:05,380
Three parts of one useful sign.

163
00:10:05,630 --> 00:10:08,890
And the right side of the street.

164
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:13,690
All three match the library trip we wanted
this morning.

165
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,470
Saturday, northbound, nine fifty.

166
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,120
All on the same line.

167
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:24,060
My original number finally has the right
company.

168
00:10:24,310 --> 00:10:29,290
We didn't change the time. Just where we wait
for it.

169
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,197
This bench feels just as comfortable.

170
00:10:33,447 --> 00:10:37,374
Comfortable is good. Going the right way helps
too.

171
00:10:37,624 --> 00:10:39,501
We have both now.

172
00:10:39,751 --> 00:10:44,498
My knees like it here as much as the other
side.

173
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,470
Six tickets, still here.

174
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,690
Three adult, three child.

175
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:54,060
And one envelope to keep the used ones
together.

176
00:10:54,310 --> 00:10:58,430
Good. Nobody has to look for small change
today.

177
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:03,550
Six dollars for adults, three for us.

178
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,484
Nine altogether.

179
00:11:05,734 --> 00:11:09,589
A clear total. I enjoy those more every day.

180
00:11:09,839 --> 00:11:14,498
And none of us has to buy a second ticket
today.

181
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:18,718
Seven, Library. The bus agrees with the stop.

182
00:11:18,968 --> 00:11:21,811
That is the last sign to check.

183
00:11:22,061 --> 00:11:25,279
Then we wait for the door to open.

184
00:11:25,529 --> 00:11:29,497
Doors first, then feet. We can see it from
here.

185
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,437
The door is open.

186
00:11:32,687 --> 00:11:35,470
And the bus is fully stopped.

187
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:39,349
Now we can go one at a time.

188
00:11:39,599 --> 00:11:44,497
Good. It looks much bigger up close than on
the leaflet.

189
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,900
Are we going on now?

190
00:11:48,150 --> 00:11:50,980
After anyone coming off has room.

191
00:11:51,230 --> 00:11:53,630
A little space helps everyone.

192
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:58,000
I'll wait right here with you until it's
clear.

193
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:04,620
Good morning. Six prepaid tickets for the
library, please.

194
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:06,840
We are all together.

195
00:12:07,090 --> 00:12:09,920
Would you count with me, Maya?

196
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:13,430
Of course. Three adults and three children.

197
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,470
One for each person.

198
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:21,840
Six checked. No extra passengers hiding in my
envelope.

199
00:12:22,090 --> 00:12:24,490
Does that leave anyone behind?

200
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:28,430
Nobody. All six tickets belong to someone
here.

201
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,437
Take the handrail, Max.

202
00:12:32,687 --> 00:12:35,893
A moving staircase that waits for us.

203
00:12:36,143 --> 00:12:39,772
This one stays still until everyone is aboard.

204
00:12:40,022 --> 00:12:44,497
Hang on until both your feet are on the bus.

205
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,470
Here is their home.

206
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:50,980
Six used tickets, back in one envelope.

207
00:12:51,230 --> 00:12:53,630
Now we need six seats.

208
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:58,000
Let's keep this aisle clear while we find
them.

209
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,300
Ella, beside me.

210
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:04,950
Leo, this pair is ours.

211
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:08,890
Dad, our seats face the correct direction too.

212
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:13,690
Lucky us. I already tried traveling the other
way today.

213
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,470
Books below, cards above.

214
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,120
And nothing in the aisle.

215
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:23,630
The books have a very tidy journey.

216
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:28,430
Good. Nobody sharing our ride has to step
around them.

217
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:33,607
Departure. From the right stop this time.

218
00:13:33,857 --> 00:13:37,784
Does the wrong stop know we changed our minds?

219
00:13:38,034 --> 00:13:40,321
It will manage without us.

220
00:13:40,571 --> 00:13:44,498
I think it's happy to have its bench back.

221
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:48,426
The bus is doing all the walking.

222
00:13:48,676 --> 00:13:51,216
And we are doing the sitting.

223
00:13:51,466 --> 00:13:55,164
I am very good at this part of traveling.

224
00:13:55,414 --> 00:13:59,498
For once, your feet don't have to lead the
way.

225
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:03,283
Pine Street comes before Oak Street.

226
00:14:03,533 --> 00:14:05,893
We can watch for it.

227
00:14:06,143 --> 00:14:09,772
And keep our bags ready without standing yet.

228
00:14:10,022 --> 00:14:14,497
I'll watch for the names while the books stay
put.

229
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:19,190
We passed the bakery a long time ago.

230
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,240
A promising development.

231
00:14:21,490 --> 00:14:23,460
Oak Street is next.

232
00:14:23,710 --> 00:14:27,830
Good. I'll keep my ears open for our stop.

233
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:34,468
How will the bus know we want to get off?

234
00:14:34,718 --> 00:14:36,436
We request the stop.

235
00:14:36,686 --> 00:14:40,279
The library is the next one on our route.

236
00:14:40,529 --> 00:14:44,497
Then how do we ask without shouting at the
driver?

237
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:47,300
Requested.

238
00:14:47,550 --> 00:14:50,380
We wait until the bus stops.

239
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:53,890
The bag can wait down here too.

240
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:58,690
Right. The bus knows where we want to get off.

241
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,300
I am ready.

242
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:06,240
Excellent. Ready can sit down for another
moment.

243
00:15:06,490 --> 00:15:09,750
That is the comfortable kind of ready.

244
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:14,120
My knees are happy to wait for the doors.

245
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,470
Blue canopy, library sign.

246
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,690
That is the place.

247
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:23,200
And the books are ready to return.

248
00:15:23,450 --> 00:15:27,570
Good. We'll take the whole family through that
door.

249
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,900
Arrival. Now we can stand.

250
00:15:33,150 --> 00:15:34,950
Folder with me.

251
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:38,460
Three books and one umbrella with me.

252
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:42,830
All six of us can get off together now.

253
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,116
Thank you. Have a good morning.

254
00:15:48,366 --> 00:15:51,777
That bus knew exactly where it was going.

255
00:15:52,027 --> 00:15:55,836
And we knew where we wanted to get off.

256
00:15:56,086 --> 00:15:59,497
That was the part I needed help with.

257
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:04,060
Here we are. Quiet voices from this door.

258
00:16:04,310 --> 00:16:07,870
My grand arrival speech can be very small.

259
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,857
Hello, books.

260
00:16:10,107 --> 00:16:14,497
You can say hello quietly. They have very good
pages.

261
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,470
Our three return books.

262
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,550
They have had a busy week.

263
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:23,630
Now someone else can enjoy them.

264
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:28,430
I wonder who'll get to take the red one next.

265
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,470
Red returned. Blue returned.

266
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:35,550
Do the books get another ticket?

267
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:39,060
Just another reader when they are ready.

268
00:16:39,310 --> 00:16:43,860
I hope they give the red one a good home.

269
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,300
Yellow returned too.

270
00:16:47,550 --> 00:16:50,810
That leaves room for three new choices.

271
00:16:51,060 --> 00:16:53,890
And time to choose them carefully.

272
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:59,120
Good. I want to look at the pictures before I
choose.

273
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,470
There are maps here.

274
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,520
And seeds.

275
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:08,460
My very large dinosaur has found a shelf.

276
00:17:08,710 --> 00:17:13,690
I like being able to see what each of you
picked.

277
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:18,040
You found the north arrow first.

278
00:17:18,290 --> 00:17:22,374
Maps work better when I know which way they
face.

279
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,392
That book suits today.

280
00:17:24,642 --> 00:17:29,498
You can teach me how to read the next map we
take.

281
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:33,265
These little seeds become all of this?

282
00:17:33,515 --> 00:17:37,009
That sounds like a good question for your
book.

283
00:17:37,259 --> 00:17:40,389
My maps can show where the plants grow.

284
00:17:40,639 --> 00:17:44,498
Maybe one day I can grow what I'm reading
about.

285
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:49,190
The dinosaur is enormous, but the book fits.

286
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,410
A very considerate dinosaur.

287
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:53,630
Shall we borrow it?

288
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:58,430
Yes, please. I think my backpack can handle
that dinosaur.

289
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,760
One book on each of your cards.

290
00:18:04,010 --> 00:18:05,810
Atlas on mine.

291
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:08,890
The plant book on mine, please.

292
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:13,690
The seeds are mine. I'll remember which card I
used.

293
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:18,330
Do we pay another nine dollars?

294
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:20,980
No. These are library loans.

295
00:18:21,230 --> 00:18:24,920
Different kind of ticket. Different kind of
journey.

296
00:18:25,170 --> 00:18:29,290
Good. We only have to bring the dinosaur back.

297
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,900
Three new books, same bag.

298
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:34,950
Umbrella still secure.

299
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:38,460
Cards and receipt in their own place.

300
00:18:38,710 --> 00:18:43,260
I like knowing which bag gets the books this
time.

301
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,607
There is a whole world in here.

302
00:18:48,857 --> 00:18:51,964
And a very small beginning in mine.

303
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:54,911
Mine begins with very large feet.

304
00:18:55,161 --> 00:18:59,498
We'll have three very different stories to
tell at home.

305
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:04,309
I liked sounding certain more than checking
the sign.

306
00:19:04,559 --> 00:19:07,573
You changed your mind when we checked.

307
00:19:07,823 --> 00:19:10,042
That helped the whole trip.

308
00:19:10,292 --> 00:19:14,499
I'd rather be the dad who asks while there's
time.

309
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,466
Your call helped us ask a clearer question.

310
00:19:18,716 --> 00:19:22,028
And your careful crossing plan got us there
safely.

311
00:19:22,278 --> 00:19:25,590
Very good company for a man with two
directions.

312
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:29,498
Let's tell Dad how the blue shelter matched
the sign.

313
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:35,089
Grandpa wanted a story. We have the stop that
did not move.

314
00:19:35,339 --> 00:19:37,374
He will enjoy that one.

315
00:19:37,624 --> 00:19:40,024
Please mention that I eventually did.

316
00:19:40,274 --> 00:19:44,498
I'll make you the one who finally read the
little line.

317
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,760
Right bus. Right direction. Very good arrival.

318
00:19:49,010 --> 00:19:51,410
And all six of us.

319
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:53,630
The dinosaur approves. Quietly.

320
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:58,000
Shh. The biggest reader has the quietest
dinosaur today.
